With her chin resting on her hand, Claudine let out a series of exaggerated sighs. Her curly brown hair flapped along with each sigh.\par
Countess Brandt frowned at her daughter and whispered, \ldblquote Claudine, please behave like a lady.\rdblquote  Her voice was full of impatience.\par
Even though Claudine was still too young to be called a lady, circumstances demanded that she behave like one.\par
Realizing how impossible this seemed for her daughter, Countess Brandt let out a long sigh. \ldblquote I\rquote m so lonely and bored,\rdblquote  Claudine grumbled.\par
The other noblewoman sitting at the tea table looked at her. Blushing with embarrassment at her daughter\rquote s childishness, Countess Brandt replied, \ldblquote Then go play with the boys.\rdblquote\par
However, Claudine didn\rquote t budge. \ldblquote They treat me like I\rquote m not even there, and they say things I can\rquote t understand.\rdblquote  Claudine\rquote s pitiful expression drew soft giggles from the noblewomen.\par
\ldblquote Well, It\rquote s natural that she would be bored. She doesn\rquote t have any friends her age,\rdblquote  said Elise von Herhardt with a nod as she petted the puppy sitting on her lap.\par
\ldblquote See, Mom? Lady Herhardt gets it!\rdblquote  Claudine exclaimed, delighted that someone was siding with her. She then turned to the garden. After a moment she pointed and asked, \ldblquote Who\rquote s that girl over there?\rdblquote\par
The noblewoman looked in the direction she was pointing, and saw a small girl following behind the gardener as he tended to the roses.\par
\par
\ldblquote Can I play with her?\rdblquote  Claudine asked. \ldblquote She looks like she\rquote s about my age.\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote I don\rquote t know, Claudine, isn\rquote t she an orphan from a foreign country? That\rquote s not the kind of child you should be making friends with,\rdblquote  Countess Brandt replied.\par
\ldblquote But I don\rquote t mind, Mom. I\rquote m sure she\rquote ll be more fun to play with than a puppy,\rdblquote  Claudine replied in a calm, confident tone beyond her years. Countess Brandt was now blushing so much that even her ears were red. Elise von Herhardt laughed delightedly and rang the bell to summon a maid. \ldblquote Bring that girl here. The one the gardener is taking care of.\rdblquote\par
\par
