At first, Layla thought that she was seeing things. This happened to her sometimes. Since her eyesight was so poor, she would occasionally see a\par
piece of fruit that had fallen on the forest path and mistake it for a squirrel or would be startled by a log floating in the water that she mistook for a person.\par
But in this case, the form she saw in the water was unmistakably human. She could tell it was a man. A tall man without any clothes on. Once his wet, black hair came into her view, she had to abandon the idea that she was seeing things.\par
There was no mistaking it. What she saw floating in the river was not an object, it was Duke Matthias von Herhardt.\par
She dropped the newspaper in shock. It fluttered down to the ground below. If she hadn\rquote t instinctively held onto the trunk of the tree, she would have followed right behind the newspaper. An inner voice started to guide her.\par
\par
Close your eyes. No, get down from the tree and go home. Or at the very least, scream. But all she could do was stare in shock at the naked man.\par
It was the same with Duke Herhardt as well. Making no attempt to hide his naked body, he was staring back at Layla as he continued to float on the water.\par
Can f he at least float downstream?! Layla thought. Just then, the duke suddenly turned his body over in the water and started swimming toward the edge of the river near where Layla was.\par
\ldblquote N-no!\rdblquote  she shouted, her clear voice reverberating far and wide. \ldblquote Don\rquote t! Don\rquote t come this way! You can\rquote t!\rdblquote  She hurriedly shuffled down the tree in a panic. She forgot proper etiquette and made no formal greeting to the duke. She also forgot her hat and her basket. She just ran. Her legs carried her down the forest path at an incredible pace. When she had made it about halfway back to the cottage, someone shouted, \ldblquote Layla!\rdblquote\par
Without slowing down, she looked and saw that it was Kyle. Having taken her eyes off the path, she started to stumble. Kyle rushed to catch her before she fell down. \ldblquote Where have you been?\rdblquote  he asked. \ldblquote You weren\rquote t at the cottage, so I\rquote ve been looking for you all over.\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote Kyle, Kyle, what should I do?\rdblquote  she muttered in a half-crazed voice as she struggled to breathe.\par
\ldblquote Why? What\rquote s going on? Did you come across a wild animal or something?\rdblquote\par
She shook her head vigorously. Even more puzzled, Kyle looked far down the path in the direction from which she had just come. There was nothing there. The forest was calm and serene as always. \ldblquote What is it, then?\rdblquote  he asked. \ldblquote Why are you in such a shock?\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote What should I do\'85?\rdblquote  she asked. Her eyes started to well up with tears, and she flopped down to sit on the ground. Lifting her apron to cover her face, she\par
\par
shook her head several times in distress. Her mind kept flashing back to what she had seen, even though she didn\rquote t want it to. Now clutching her hair, she asked, \ldblquote What should I do? What should I do, Kyle?\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote I can\rquote t answer that until you tell me what happened. So what happened?\rdblquote  he asked, furrowing his brow as he stooped down towards her.\par
After a moment, she looked up at him. Her face was as red as a well- ripened raspberry. Her lip twitched as if she was about to say something, then more tears formed in her eyes and she buried her face in her apron again.\par
At this point, Kyle couldn\rquote t help but start giggling. \ldblquote Hey, what the heck did you see? Was it a ghost or something?\rdblquote\par
No, it was something scarier than that, she wanted to answer. But when she tried to speak, all that came out of her mouth were hot gasps of air.\par
