\ldblquote I feel like I\rquote m gazing into a new world,\rdblquote  Layla whispered in a daze.\par
The gray-haired optician let out a friendly chuckle. \ldblquote Considering how bad your eyesight was, I can believe it. It must\rquote ve been quite hard for you.\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote No, it wasn\rquote t too bad, other than when I was trying to read,\rdblquote  she cheerfully replied as she took off the glasses and put them on again. When she did so, the blurry world miraculously became clear. She still hadn\rquote t gotten over her amazement at this.\par
She had turned the heaps of raspberries she had gathered from the forest into jam, which she had then sold. As soon as she had saved up enough money to purchase eyeglasses, she had ridden her bicycle into the city. She had no trouble locating the optician\rquote s shop, because she had gazed longingly into its window many times before.\par
After chatting with the optician a bit more, she left the shop. The incredibly clear world around her seemed new and wondrous.\par
With each step she took, she discovered another detail of this new world. She was filled with love and gratitude for the wild raspberries growing in the Arvis forest that had enabled this. She also felt proud of herself for all the hard work she had put in, not only picking them, but also standing in front of a hot stove, stirring the jam until her arm felt like it was going to fall off.\par
But why, at such a wonderful time as this, do those indecent memories keep flashing into my mind? she thought, frowning as she tried to clear her mind of the memory of when she had unintentionally seen the duke\rquote s naked body.\par
\par
She had been so flustered and frightened that day, she had waited until dusk to go fetch her basket. By that point in the evening, the forest was quiet, and the river was flowing calmly. The stillness of the area finally brought her relief, and she grabbed her hat and basket and went on her way. However, her cheeks still felt hot. She was so distracted, she didn\rquote t even feel the weight of the full basket in her arms. After that day, she had felt awkward around men, including even Bill and Kyle.\par
Even if it\rquote s his land, why would the duke swim naked in broad daylight? She shook her head to try to rid herself of the unpleasant memory. I\rquote d better not go back to the river until the duke leaves Arvis again.\par
Having made this resolution, she started walking again, when she heard a familiar voice.\par
\ldblquote Layla\'85?\rdblquote\par
The loud, high-pitched voice sounded just like that of Claudine von Brandt.\par
Oh my. The time has come. Layla paused for a moment to catch her breath, and, putting on a polite smile, she slowly turned around.\par
However, much to her surprise, the person she saw was none other than the man who had been causing her mind so much distress, Duke Herhardt.\par
He was standing right there, in the midst of this newly-clear world. She was so startled that it took her a moment to notice Claudine standing next to him. Claudine had stopped visiting Arvis while Duke Herhardt had been away serving in the military, so Layla hadn\rquote t seen her in a long time. During that time, Claudine had transformed into a perfect noblewoman.\par
Layla politely curtsied, and the other two gracefully nodded back at her. \ldblquote Since when have you worn glasses? I almost didn\rquote t recognize you,\rdblquote  Claudine said. Layla had hoped that they would have simply walked on without saying\par
\par
anything, but now she had no choice but to continue smiling politely at Claudine, while being careful not to look at Duke Herhardt at all.\par
\ldblquote Have you been well?\rdblquote  Claudine asked, looking closely at Layla with narrowed eyes.\par
\ldblquote Yes, Miss.\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote We were just on our way to have some tea,\rdblquote  Claudine said, smiling as she glanced over at the hotel across the street. Layla deliberated over the proper response.\par
Should I say, \ldblquote Yes, Miss\rdblquote\'85? Or maybe, \ldblquote Is that so, Miss?\rdblquote\par
Before Layla had a chance to say anything, Claudine took mercy on her and said, \ldblquote You should come along with us, Layla.\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote Pardon?\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote It\rquote s been so long since we\rquote ve seen each other, I\rquote d love to have a cup of tea with you. Is that all right with you, Duke Herhardt?\rdblquote\par
Matthias smiled subtly to indicate his consent. Layla noted to herself that Claudine hadn\rquote t asked if it was all right with her. This was nothing new, of course.\par
Matthias and Claudine continued walking. Their attendants, who had been waiting nearby, followed behind them. Layla let out a sigh and turned her bicycle around. The creaking of her worn-out wheels blended with the clicking of the nobles\rquote  expensive shoes.\par
