\ldblquote She\rquote s grown a lot, hasn\rquote t she? She looks like a lady now,\rdblquote  Claudine commented as she watched Layla leave. She sounded like a mother talking about her daughter, even though she was only one year older.\par
\ldblquote That\rquote s because she is one,\rdblquote  Matthias replied, smiling slightly.\par
\ldblquote Yes, I suppose you\rquote re right. She is old enough to be called a lady,\rdblquote  Claudine replied before sinking into thought. After a moment, she smiled brightly and deftly changed the subject, saying, \ldblquote Oh, by the way, did you hear that Riette bought a marvelous new car?\rdblquote\par
They continued their aristocratic conversation. It was as if Layla had never even been there. However, she soon showed up once again in an unexpected location.\par
Matthias was on his way back to Arvis with Claudine after the relaxing teatime. While sitting in stopped traffic, he gazed out the window from his seat in the back of the car, and there was Layla, walking her bicycle as she strolled down the road with a boy. It must have been the friend she was going to meet.\par
The boy\rquote s face looked familiar. After a moment, Matthias realized who he was. It was the family doctor\rquote s son. He was fairly sure his name was Kyle Ettman.\par
Layla shouted something at the boy after he repeatedly tapped her glasses with his finger. This only caused the boy to double down on his mischievousness. Eventually, Layla sighed and started laughing.\par
\par
The two spent a while laughing and chatting playfully before coming to a stop in front of the front stairs of the library. Layla put down her bicycle\rquote s kickstand and sat on the bottom of the steps. Kyle took a paper bag out of the basket he was holding, then sat down next to her. He reached into the bag and took out two bottles of soda water and a sandwich. The two shared the snack as they sat next to each other. Whenever the boy spoke, Layla would laugh, and whenever she laughed, he would laugh as well.\par
Meanwhile, the traffic began to move, and Matthias turned to face forward again. Claudine, who had been looking out the window on her side of the car, turned to look at him. They smiled at each other and then resumed their amiable conversation. After a while, Matthias\rquote s thoughts drifted from the conversation back to the teatime. It occurred to him that Layla had not touched her teacup once. She had sat with her hands on her lap the entire time before quietly departing.\par
She left me to go see that boy.\par
Brooding on this thought, he was reminded of the anxious, uncomfortable look on her face when she had been staring at him.\par
It must have been because she wanted to go see the boy.\par
He then recalled the hurried way she had left the patio, almost as if she were making an escape.\par
She was fleeing from me to rush to meet him.\par
The car had now made it to Platanus Road, which led to Arvis. As they passed by the spot about halfway down the road where Layla had fallen off her bicycle, Matthias thought to himself, Layla Llewellyn is nothing to me\'85 So why is she making me feel this way?\par
