\ldblquote Since you got the sandwich, dessert is on me,\rdblquote  Layla cheerfully said as she rose from the library steps. She picked up the empty paper bag and bottles and placed them in her bicycle\rquote s basket.\par
\ldblquote Don\rquote t worry about it. I\rquote m not stingy about things like that,\rdblquote  Kyle replied with a bashful smile as he hopped onto Layla\rquote s bicycle.\par
Layla sat on the bicycle\rquote s back seat. Kyle could feel her body\rquote s warmth even in the heat of the midday sun.\par
His own body temperature started to rise, so he started to turn the pedals, hoping that the breeze would cool him down. She lightly held onto his shirt with her fingers as they rode. He wished that she would put her arms around his torso, but he didn\rquote t dare ask her to. Even so, he couldn\rquote t help but smile at the feeling of her closeness to him.\par
He had intentionally left his own bicycle at home that day, because he had wanted to ride on her bicycle with her. However, he was sure she didn\rquote t realize this.\par
\ldblquote You know what, Kyle?\rdblquote  she said, her soft voice mixing with the ticking sound of the bicycle\rquote s chain.\par
\ldblquote What?\rdblquote  Kyle replied. His knuckles were white with anticipation as he gripped the handlebars.\par
\ldblquote I\rquote m going to buy you dessert anyway. Ice cream sounds good?\rdblquote\par
Kyle chuckled. He had thought she was going to say something serious. \ldblquote Be honest, you\rquote re just offering because you feel like eating ice cream yourself,\par
\par
aren\rquote t you?\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote No, that\rquote s not it\'85\rdblquote  she replied unconvincingly.\par
Kyle steered in the direction of the cafe that he and Layla often stopped at on the way home from school. As he was putting down the kickstand, she strolled into the cafe ahead of him. Rather than follow her in, he decided to wait for her outside in the cool shade of the awning. After a short while, she reemerged, holding two vanilla ice cream cones.\par
They enjoyed their cones as they stood next to one another. It was an everyday activity that they had repeated countless times, and yet it all felt new to Kyle. He could barely take his eyes off of her. It must be her new glasses, he thought. Unable to stand it anymore, he whispered, \ldblquote Layla.\rdblquote\par
