The cottage was empty when Kyle arrived. Layla and Bill seemed to have gone out to the garden. He considered going there to look for them, then changed his mind and sat on a chair on the porch.\par
The image of Layla wearing her new glasses flashed into his mind and brought a wry smile to his face. The future Lady Ettman was pretty even with glasses. It had taken him some time to get used to her new appearance, but\par
\par
now his heart started pounding when he thought of her, just like it had always done in the past.\par
Realizing that he was starting to blush, he cleared his throat to calm himself down. Just then, Layla and Bill returned to the cottage.\par
\ldblquote What\rquote s with the hat?\rdblquote  Kyle asked, furrowing his brow at the sight of the homely, unstylish hat that was blocking Layla\rquote s face from his view. \ldblquote You look like a country bumpkin. Don\rquote t tell me you paid money for that thing,\rdblquote  he teased. Layla and Bill both reacted by scowling at Kyle.\par
\ldblquote Uncle Bill bought it for me!\rdblquote  Layla shouted, frowning. Bill silently took the shovel out of the wheelbarrow he had just brought back from the garden.\par
\ldblquote You know, now that I look at it again, it\rquote s pretty. Yep, it\rquote s really stylish! Bill has really good taste!\rdblquote  Kyle said, hurrying to amend his previous opinion.\par
\ldblquote Don\rquote t make fun of it. It\rquote s really precious to me,\rdblquote  Layla said, still sulking as she took off the gaudy straw hat, which was covered with ribbons and artificial flowers.\par
While Bill put away his wheelbarrow, Layla started making lunch. She had neatly placed the hat on one end of the table. Kyle sat down in front of it and glanced at Layla. \ldblquote Layla, are you mad at\par
\ldblquote Yep,\rdblquote  she curtly replied, dropping his plate in front of him.\par
Well, at least she\rquote s still feeding me, he thought, feeling somewhat relieved. \ldblquote I\rquote m sorry. Do you think I would\rquote ve said that if I\rquote d known your uncle got it for you?\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote I honestly don\rquote t know.\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote Why did he buy you a hat all of a sudden, anyway?\rdblquote  \ldblquote Because I asked him for one.\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote You did? You know how to ask for stuff?\rdblquote  Kyle asked in amazement. He could hardly remember Layla ever asking for something before.\par
\par
\ldblquote He was really upset about my glasses,\rdblquote  Layla said, lowering her voice. \ldblquote Ah, he was upset that your eyesight had gotten so bad?\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote No, not that. He was upset that I saved up all that money to buy these expensive glasses without telling him.\rdblquote  Having finished setting the table, she sat down across from Kyle.\par
The day Layla had returned to the cottage wearing her new glasses, Bill had reacted with shock as if he had been stabbed in the back. After listening to her explain how she had managed to acquire them, he stared at her with a frigid expression. It was the first time she had seen him upset in this way.\par
\ldblquote Layla, do you really trust me that little?\rdblquote  he had sadly asked, sighing.\par
This had made Layla feel awful. She tried to reassure him by saying that it wasn\rquote t that she didn\rquote t trust him, but rather that she had felt ashamed after all he had already done for her, and so had wanted to buy them herself. This only made him grow sadder, however.\par
After that day, things had felt a bit awkward between them. Bill had sullenly stopped speaking much, while Layla had grown very uneasy, not sure what to say or do.\par
The solution she finally came up with was the hat. \ldblquote Uncle Bill, would you buy me a hat?\rdblquote she had suddenly asked a few days earlier at the dinner table. \ldblquote I\rquote d love it so much if you\rquote d buy me a pretty hat. \rdblquote\par
Bill had chuckled at her solemn tone. But the following evening, on his way back from buying some pruning shears downtown, he bought her a straw hat covered with flowers and ribbons. Holding it out to her, he had casually said, \ldblquote I bought it at Lind\rquote s, so if you don\rquote t like it, you can go there and exchange it for a different one. \rdblquote\par
\ldblquote Did you pick it out yourself?\rdblquote  \ldblquote Well, sure I did. \rdblquote\par
\par
\ldblquote It\rquote s very pretty. \rquote\rquote Smiling brightly, she had tried on the hat.\par
Bill had purchased many items for Layla over the years, but rather than picking them out himself, he had usually either brought Layla to the store with him or asked Chef Mona to take care of it. Thus, Layla keenly felt how big of a gesture it was that he had picked out a woman\rquote s hat for her all by himself. It made her feel loved.\par
Flowers were the prettiest thing in the world to him. Thus a hat covered with flowers had to be the world\rquote s prettiest hat. This was the simple logic he had used in selecting the hat for her.\par
\ldblquote Hey! You should\rquote ve told me all that before,\rdblquote  Kyle exclaimed, feeling very ashamed after hearing Layla tell him the story behind the hat. \ldblquote I feel like trash now after making fun of that gift!\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote When would I have told you? You made fun of it as soon as you saw it.\rdblquote  \ldblquote Well sure, but\'85\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote You insolent loafer!\rdblquote  Bill shouted as he strode through the door. \ldblquote You\rquote re eating all my food again! One of these days I\rquote m going to ask Dr. Ettman to pay me back!\rdblquote\par
Kyle was frightened by his threatening tone, but when he looked at his face, he was relieved to see a friendly, playful expression. Noticing the hat sitting on the table, Bill chuckled sheepishly. Seeing Layla smiling sweetly at Bill, Kyle almost felt jealous for a moment.\par
Any man who loved Layla Llewellyn would have to settle for second place in her heart. First place would always be reserved for Uncle Bill.\par
Comforting himself with this thought, Kyle picked up his fork and started eating. He was never bothered by Bill\rquote s taunts. Layla\rquote s cooking was delicious enough that he could easily endure them.\par
