After lunch, Bill returned to work, leaving Kyle and Layla alone in the cottage. Layla sat on the porch, as usual, reading. Kyle pretended to read while actually gazing at Layla. Layla\rquote s eyes remained glued to the page, besides when she occasionally picked up a biscuit to take a bite.\par
I shouldn\rquote t have lent her that novel, Kyle thought, chuckling to himself bitterly. But my gosh, I bet she has no idea how pretty she looks concentrating on that book, or chewing on that biscuit\'85 Should I tell her howl feel today?\par
He set his book on the floor and stared at her with a serious expression. He had planned to wait a bit longer before telling her, but now he was starting to doubt himself.\par
The lightest brush of her hand against his arm made his heart feel like it was going to explode. His whole body felt hot whenever he was around her. Sometimes he had dreams about her that made him feel guilty.\par
More than that, he felt a constant sense of dread that someone would appear one day and steal her away from him. That was why he was contemplating throwing caution to the wind and confessing his feelings for her right then.\par
But just as he was about to do it, they were interrupted by the sound of a horse slowly approaching. He turned his head and saw Duke Herhardt in full riding apparel, sitting on top of a horse. Layla, who had been about to take a bite of her biscuit, looked at him in surprise.\par
\par
The duke brought his horse to a stop in front of the porch\rquote s railing. His gaze briefly paused on Kyle, before moving to rest on Layla\rquote s perplexed, blushing face.\par
