giving Layla any time to respond.\par
Layla sighed as she looked down at her blouse and skirt, which were covered with biscuit crumbs. She frantically brushed them off, but was unable to brush away the embarrassment she was feeling.\par
\ldblquote Uh, Layla, I think you got all the crumbs. You can stop,\rdblquote  Kyle said, snickering.\par
\ldblquote Why did he have to appear at a time like this?\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote What\rquote s the big deal? Don\rquote t you think the duke eats snacks like everybody else?\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote Well sure, but\'85\rdblquote  Layla muttered, unwittingly rubbing her lips again. \ldblquote Why do you care when you\rquote re always stuffing your face in front of me?\rdblquote  \ldblquote It\rquote s different with you. You\rquote re my friend.\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote And Duke Herhardt is a stranger. You shouldn\rquote t worry more about how you appear in front of a stranger than a friend.\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote Maybe you\rquote re right\'85 I don\rquote t know, though. I just feel uncomfortable around him,\rdblquote  she said, frowning.\par
\ldblquote Why? Did something happen between you two?\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote No, it\rquote s not that\'85 He just always makes me feel uncomfortable and tense.\par
I can\rquote t explain it. He just does. I don\rquote t like it.\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote What about me? You feel comfortable around me, right?\rdblquote  Kyle asked, his voice full of subtle anticipation.\par
Layla laughed dismissively as she put on her hat. \ldblquote Of course, Mr. Ettman.\rdblquote\par
Kyle\rquote s smile widened at this reply. \ldblquote Good, I thought so. Hey, you want some help picking those roses?\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote No, I can handle it myself. You should head home now.\rdblquote  \ldblquote No, I can wait here.\rdblquote\par
\par
\ldblquote Come on, Kyle. If your father finds out you were hanging out here again he\rquote ll be furious! He might even get mad at me. Go home and study.\rdblquote\par
Kyle frowned. He wanted to argue, but he knew she was right. He took a careful look in the direction the duke had ridden off in. Why do I feel so anxious? Have I been oversensitive lately? Not wanting to scare Layla by saying something needless, he kept his mouth shut. But it\rquote s not just any guy, it\rquote s Duke Herhardt, the flawless nobleman whose engagement is about to be announced. Soon, his anxiety got the better of him, and he found himself shouting, \ldblquote Layla!\rdblquote\par
Layla, who was walking towards the rose garden with basket and clippers in hand, turned and smiled, shouting, \ldblquote See you tomorrow, Kyle!\rdblquote\par
Don\rquote t go, he wanted to say. Swallowing those words, he simply waved. It\rquote s okay. It\rquote s Duke Herhardt. Nothing\rquote s going to happen. Repeating this thought to himself over and over, he watched Layla continue to walk away towards the rose garden.\par
