The cabin had large windows on all sides, affording a magnificent view of the river and the forest. Opening these windows provided cross-\par
ventilation that usually kept the interior feeling cool even in the summer.\par
However, today was an especially hot day. It was not a day when one would expect to feel chills, and yet Layla felt a chill run down her spine, causing her shoulders to shudder. She was determined to eat the food in front of her as fast as possible so she could leave, but so far she had not taken a single bite.\par
She didn\rquote t feel like eating anything. She had already eaten a large lunch and a snack after that. Moreover, laboring in the hot sun had made her lose whatever slight appetite she might have had left. Matthias had already shifted his focus from her back onto his work, but she was still having trouble breathing properly.\par
\par
Is he punishing me for doing a poor job at the errand and the flower arrangement? Layla wondered as she bit off a small piece of the sandwich. If that was his goal, he has succeeded. I certainly feel like I\rquote m being punished.\par
As she slowly chewed the piece of sandwich, she felt like spitting it out. To combat this urge, she took a sip of lemonade. She then wiped the moisture from her hands onto her apron and picked up the sandwich again. She lowered the brim of her hat to hide what she was sure was an agonized look on her face.\par
Just then, a long finger touched her chin. \ldblquote Layla, if you\rquote re a lady,\rdblquote  Matthias said, untying the ribbon under her chin as he spoke, \ldblquote then you should remove your hat when you\rquote re indoors.\rdblquote  Before she could respond, he took her straw hat off her head.\par
Layla reflexively bolted out of her seat, knocking a piece of the sandwich to the floor. Matthias narrowed his eyes, but Layla didn\rquote t notice. Her attention was fixed solely on her hat. \ldblquote P-please give it back.\rdblquote  Her voice was trembling, not with fear but with anger. \ldblquote Will you please give it back to me, Your Grace? I\rquote m going to leave now. I want to go home. Give me back my hat, please.\rdblquote\par
Matthias gripped the hat more tightly to indicate that he had no intention of returning it to her. All I did was take her hat, he thought. Why is she reacting like she\rquote s been stripped naked? He noticed with amusement that she was blushing. It seemed that her skin was quick to react to minor things. \ldblquote Eat,\rdblquote  he said, pointing to the two remaining pieces of sandwich on her plate. \ldblquote Eat, and you\rquote ll get your hat back and you can go home. It\rquote s simple.\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote No, I don\rquote t want to,\rdblquote  she said, shaking her head as she approached him. \ldblquote I don\rquote t feel like eating. I can\rquote t stomach anything right now. I hate it.\rdblquote  Her frightened eyes were quivering. She was amazed to hear the bold words coming out of her mouth.\par
\par
Matthias tightened his grip on the hat and stood up from his seat. Looming over her ominously, he asked, \ldblquote You hate it?\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote I\rquote m sorry for everything. Please give me back my hat. Okay?\rdblquote  Standing on her tiptoes, she reached for the hat. She was on the verge of tears.\par
Keeping his eyes fixed on her face, Matthias slowly extended his arms and held the hat tantalizingly above her head. Layla watched closely as he did so, then shifted her gaze to look him in the eye.\par
After a brief, tense moment, Matthias proceeded to toss the hat out the window. The hat was swept up by the breeze and flew onto the surface of the river. Layla gave him an icy-cold scowl, then frantically ran out of the room.\par
Matthias walked to the window looking out onto the dock and river. Layla soon appeared on the dock. At first trying to reach the floating hat with her foot, she soon removed her apron and glasses and set them down on the dock.\par
Is she really going to jump into the river just to get that stupid hat? Matthias wondered, looking down at her with delight.\par
Despite her bold actions, Layla was visibly shaking, as if she were afraid of the water.\par
