least, this had been his plan until he stepped out of the mansion. All of a sudden, however, he looked around and realized that he was standing on the road leading to the gardener\rquote s cottage. He paused for a moment but didn\rquote t turn back.\par
Everything had proceeded in an orderly manner for the previous several days. It had to. The irritation he was feeling would be resolved by her tears.\par
Lengthening his stride, he started down the shady forest path. He loosened his tie and undid the top button on his tight- fitting shirt. His movements were rougher and more impetuous than usual. His emotions had been getting increasingly difficult to manage, and he was sick of it. He wanted everything in\par
\par
his world to be in its place. His emotions were no exception. This was the reason he had never allowed himself to obsess over women.\par
As far as he was concerned, sexual desire was nothing more than a base instinct. He had never been swayed by it enough to form an attachment. Rather, he thought it was best to satisfy it and be done with it, to prevent it from becoming too much of a burden. Such desires had never occupied his mind much in the first place.\par
This made him feel all the more displeasure at the emotions he was feeling about Layla. She was all he saw in the world. All his senses were focused on her. He could feel an uncontrollable passion building up from deep inside himself. Sometimes he was unable to stop his lustful thoughts about her.\par
He became distraught the moment that he realized he was in the grip of these feelings. They weren\rquote t even worthy of going on his list of priorities. Layla Llewellyn wasn\rquote t either. This seemed obvious to him. Still, he wanted to make sure.\par
The shade over the forest path lessened as he drew nearer to the cottage. Soon he could see the blinding light of the summer sun beyond the edge of the forest. Without hesitation, he walked into the light.\par
