Ever since she was young, she had had a habit of assuming the worst. Since facing misfortune without preparation or defense could be fatal, she thought she could better face whatever misfortune might befall her if she thought about all possibilities beforehand and prepared for them.\par
As soon as any of her relatives started looking at her disapprovingly, she would start preparing herself for the inevitable consequences. If they hit her,\par
\par
she wouldn\rquote t cry. If they yelled at her, she wouldn\rquote t let it hurt her feelings. When they finally sent her away, she would take it in stride, and politely bid them farewell. On the way to the next home, she would try to smile even more brightly.\par
Her efforts had been successful, with each new home, she had been a little less affected by their abuse, and had smiled a little more brightly. Misfortunes had continued lo follow her wherever she went, but thanks to her preparation, she had gotten much better at enduring them. But if some misfortune had befallen Uncle Bill, she didn\rquote t think she could take it in stride.\par
