Compared to the beautiful garden and forest on the sprawling land of the renowned Arvis estate, this mansion\rquote s garden was more modest. Since the mansion was located in the middle of the city, the garden was naturally smaller, and neither Matthias nor any of the previous dukes had been particularly interested in landscaping.\par
Thus, the Ratse mansion\rquote s garden was simple, in keeping with the simple architecture and decor of the mansion itself. However, each year when the rose season arrived, a large quantity of roses were transported from Arvis to the\par
\par
Ratse mansion\rquote s garden, temporarily transforming the small garden into a spectacular sight to see.\par
A passing breeze carried the scent of the roses up to Matthias\rquote s room, and he thought about the upcoming summer break when he would return to Arvis. While thinking of this, his mind suddenly drifted to thoughts of Layla helping the gardener with various tasks throughout each summer day. He frowned.\par
She always smelled like roses. Like the roses that the master gardener plants. The most beautiful roses in the world. Little had Matthias expected that his downfall would come from something else raised by the gardener; Layla, a girl who was nothing. What\rquote s in a name?\par
He closed the window and turned around. His wet hair dripped on his feet.\par
It seems that things have turned out rather well for her. Normally a girl like her wouldn\rquote t dream of being able to marry a doctor\rquote s son. Thanks to Kyle Ettman\rquote s foolish love, she\rquote s going to become Mrs. Ettman, and will even attend college here in the capital. She\rquote s remarkably lucky.\par
