If that beautiful nuisance were to disappear from his sight, it would benefit him as well. For this reason, he should have been in full support of her marriage. However, even after closing the window, the scent of roses still lingered in his nose. After a moment, he realized that this was because there was a vase of roses on the credenza in his room. They looked to be roses from the garden.\par
He turned away from the vase to look at the golden birdcage in another corner of the room, before turning back to the vase.\par
\ldblquote Layla.\rdblquote  Speaking the name at full volume, it sounded even sweeter to his ears. It\rquote s rose season, but you \rquote re not here.\par
\par
Still lost in reminiscence, he reached out and grabbed the roses from the vase. They were a pale shade of pink, just like the color of Layla\rquote s cheeks when she was crying. He gripped the roses tighter, crushing them.\par
It\rquote s good that things have turned out this way, he thought. He wanted to believe this. But\'85 His eyes slowly narrowed. Can there really be a rose season without you? I always return to Anus when the roses are in bloom. Could it really be that you won\rquote t be there?\par
The doubts that followed these thoughts led him to an unexpected realization, that she had always been there in the garden during the summers when the roses were in full bloom. It was like she was a part of Arvis. Which also meant that she was his.\par
Having torn the roses out of the vase and crushed them, he couldn\rquote t bring himself to throw them aside. Just then, his bird started singing. At the same moment, for the first time in his life, he felt the desire to kill someone. This desire felt clear as day to him. What wasn\rquote t clear, however, was who it was directed towards the doctor\rquote s son, or her.\par
