The museum seemed no less massive on the second visit. Looking around with just as much wonder as on the first day she had gone there, Layla took in the sight of the impressive building housing the Berg Empire\rquote s natural history museum.\par
The day after they arrived in Ratse, the first place Kyle had taken Layla was this museum. Located across the street from each other, Ratse\rquote s art museum and natural history museum were among the capital city\rquote s most popular tourist destinations. Layla was used to Karlsbar, a city just as large and prosperous as Ratse. But standing in between these two magnificent museums, she was spellbound, Karlsbar had nothing of the sort.\par
Friends of hers from school who had visited the capital had all gushed over the beautiful art museum. But for Layla, the choice to visit the natural history museum first had been a no-brainer. Just as Kyle had predicted, it was like heaven to her. The only problem was that it was too big to see all its exhibits in one day.\par
She had figured that after devoting an entire day to wandering its halls, she would need to spend another full day there before there they left Ratse to see everything. She walked excitedly into the museum\rquote s lobby.\par
