Layla looked like a girl headed out to a picnic.\par
Matthias gazed at her as she excitedly walked from exhibit to exhibit without any sign of slowing down.\par
He had already been confident that the woman he saw was Layla before she entered the natural history museum, but he had still decided to follow her in, keeping his distance. Even after having satisfied his curiosity about what she was doing, he wanted to keep observing her for a bit longer.\par
Then it occurred to him that it was the time of year when the college entrance exam was being held in Ratse. If she had come to the capital to take the exam, it meant that she must have made up her mind to go to college after all. Which meant she had probably decided to marry Kyle Ettman as well.\par
She was standing in front of a glass display case filled with various plant specimens, intently jotting something down in her notebook. There was an\par
\par
enraptured smile on her face, as if she were looking at a rare gemstone or something.\par
Matthias had no idea what it was about the plant specimens that could possibly be making her smile like that. He considered approaching her, then decided to stand back and watch for a bit longer. Once he approached, he knew she would stop smiling. With his hands behind his back, he continued to follow her.\par
For the most part, she seemed not to have changed much since the previous summer when he had last seen her, but there were some subtle differences. Her face looked more slender, her expression looked more relaxed, and her movements looked more graceful. Wearing a white dress with lace trim, she looked more mature as well.\par
After spending a long time looking at everything, she left the plant specimen exhibit and started walking down the passageway to the next exhibit room, when she suddenly stopped in her tracks. Matthias knew the reason for this at once.\par
The passageway was like heaven. It was decorated with silver-painted tree branches that had white feathers attached to them like leaves. Hanging from the branches were multi-colored crystal ornaments shaped like birds. The light reflecting off them gave the passageway a dream-like quality.\par
She marveled at the sight. \ldblquote Wow\'85\rdblquote  Matthias heard her innocent exclamation.\par
Watching her run excitedly around the passageway, he couldn\rquote t help but grin. Her thick blonde hair and lacy white dress fluttered as she ran about like a little girl.\par
She then came to a stop in the middle of that wondrous passageway and, standing on her tiptoes, reached out to try to touch one of the ornaments, but\par
\par
the bird remained tantalizingly just beyond her fingertips.\par
As she continued to gasp in amazement with her head raised to look at the ceiling, Matthias started to walk towards her. Before she had noticed that anyone was there, he had come up behind her, put his arms around her waist, and lifted her off the ground.\par
Startled, she turned her head to look around, but she was already floating in mid-air. The crystal bird that she had been unable to reach was now glittering right in front of her eyes. She felt like a bird flying through the spring sky, able to go wherever it wanted. It was a strange, beautiful, dream- like feeling.\par
Matthias then casually set her back down on the ground. The skirt of her dress ballooned out, then slowly descended, gently tickling her calves.\par
The sensation of touching the crystal bird still lingered in her hands. Hiding her hands behind her back, she looked up in a daze. Matthias slowly removed his officer\rquote s cap. The same blue eyes she had seen that late-summer afternoon the previous year were looking at her.\par
