a little upset that that last coin he gave me missed the basin after I wished that I would never see him again.\par
After leaving Arvis the previous summer, he had not visited at all for an entire year. She had assumed this pattern would continue until his military service was complete. As long as she moved away from Arvis before then, her wish would have come true.\par
Shaking her head, she stepped out of the cottage into the backyard. Maybe my wish will come true anyway. The duke is returning, but I\rquote m moving away from here.\par
Breathing a sigh of relief, she tended to the animals and the vegetable garden. Just as she was finishing up her morning chores, her pigeon Phoebe returned from the Ettmans\rquote  house. A note from Kyle was wrapped around her ankle: My mom wants to invite you to dinner tonight. See, Layla? I was right!\par
She felt like she could hear Kyle\rquote s voice behind the words of the note.\par
To calm Layla\rquote s concerns, he had guaranteed that his mother was going to come around to liking her eventually. He had assured her that everything was going to turn out all right, that by the fall they would be a married couple strolling the university campus together. They would be happy, very happy.\par
\ldblquote Uncle Bill, I\rquote m going to go to the Ettmans\rquote  for dinner tonight,\rdblquote  she said, hurrying towards Bill as he arrived back at the cottage. \ldblquote Mrs. Ettman invited me.\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote See, Layla?\rdblquote  he cheerfully replied, saying the same thing Kyle had said in his note. \ldblquote Didn\rquote t I tell you everything would turn out all right?\rdblquote\par
She smiled at the sight of his smile. Her heart was pounding, which she chalked up to the excitement.\par
