Matthias returned to Arvis late one afternoon. As his car pulled up in front of the mansion, a sense of nervous anticipation spread throughout the staff members lined up to greet him.\par
His reception was nothing out of the ordinary. He was politely greeted by all the staff, as well as his joyful grandmother and smiling mother.\par
Out of habit, as he passed by the gardener, he looked down at the ground. Next to the large boots, the gardener was wearing, there was a small pair of feet in simple brown shoes. Layla Llewellyn was always by Bill Remmer\rquote s side. He knew this would no longer be the case after this summer, however.\par
He passed by the gardener without turning his head. He was looking forward, in the direction of the staircase at the far end of the mansion\rquote s main hall.\par
\ldblquote I see your bird has returned with you as well,\rdblquote  Elise von Herhardt remarked with a laugh as she saw a servant holding the golden birdcage that housed the canary that her son had taken with him when he had left Arvis the previous summer. \ldblquote How strange. You never wanted a puppy or any other pet as a child, and now you cherish that bird so much.\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote If you\rquote re interested in birds now, why don\rquote t we expand the greenhouse and bring in some more different types of birds?\rdblquote  Dowager Herhardt suggested, smiling.\par
\ldblquote That won\rquote t be necessary, Grandmother,\rdblquote  Matthias replied, smiling back at her. \ldblquote One is enough for me.\rdblquote  After this dry response, he walked into the\par
\par
mansion. Before ascending the staircase, he looked up at the grand chandelier, and at the Herhardt family crest imprinted on the ceiling. He had been born underneath that crest, he was living underneath that crest, and one day he would draw his last breath underneath that crest. This fact felt entirely natural to him. He lowered his gaze again and walked up the stairs.\par
