\ldblquote Linda, do you know what you\rquote re saying right now?\rdblquote  Daniel Raynor asked in disbelief. The rays of the setting sun flowing in through the uncurtained window made him squint as he sat across from his cousin, Linda Ettman. \ldblquote Linda!\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote Lower your voice, Daniel,\rdblquote  she said. Her face remained amazingly calm as she glanced at the closed door.\par
Daniel let out a distressed moan. After a failed investment in an overseas mining venture had caused his financial situation to go downhill quickly, he had gone several times to ask for help from his richest relative, his cousin Linda Ettman. Each time he had asked, she had given him a cold yet graceful rejection. But much to his surprise, this time she had come to see him and offer to help him willingly.\par
Of course, he hadn\rquote t expected the help to come for free. But when he heard what she wanted him to do in exchange, it made him hesitate, despite the dire straits he was in. \ldblquote That\rquote s stealing, Linda. How could I\'85.\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote No,\rdblquote  Mrs. Ettman said, cutting him off. She slowly closed and opened her eyes, then said, \ldblquote It\rquote s just briefly hiding something and then putting it back.\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote But\'85\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote Don\rquote t you care about Kyle?\rdblquote\par
\par
\ldblquote Of course I do.\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote And you need my help, don\rquote t you?\rdblquote  She lifted her hands from her lap and rubbed her temples.\par
Daniel\rquote s face started to flush, but he stopped trying to argue, just as she knew he would.\par
\ldblquote You\rquote ll take the money, and then when the time comes, you\rquote ll put it back. That\rquote s it. By doing that simple favor for me, you\rquote ll be able to protect your family, and I\rquote ll be able to protect my son.\rdblquote  Straightening her posture, she looked into his eyes. \ldblquote Sounds like a pretty good deal to me. What do you think, Daniel?\rdblquote\par
