When Kyle saw Layla coming down the forest path towards him, a smile as warm as the sunset spread across his face. \ldblquote Layla!\rdblquote\par
She had been looking at her feet as she walked, but when she heard him shouting her name, she looked up at once. Her eyes widened when she saw him. He felt boundless love for her when he saw her increase her pace while smiling at him.\par
\ldblquote When did you get here?\rdblquote  she asked.\par
\ldblquote A little while ago. I went to the cottage, and Bill said that you\rquote d been summoned to go to the mansion, so I thought I\rquote d come rescue you.\par
\ldblquote Rescue me?\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote It\rquote s obvious why Lady Claudine summoned you, isn\rquote t it?\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote It wasn\rquote t that today.\rdblquote  She smiled as she started walking again. Matching her pace, he started walking alongside her.\par
\par
\ldblquote And it wasn\rquote t Lady Claudine who summoned me. It was Dowager Herhardt.\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote Dowager Herhardt? She summoned you?\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote Yeah. She congratulated me on getting into college, and asked if there was any gift I wanted.\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote What did you say?\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote That I didn\rquote t want anything, that I was just grateful that they had let me stay here.\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote That\rquote s a very Layla-like response,\rdblquote  he replied, chuckling at her predictable reply.\par
He furtively reached over to hold her hand. Unlike before, she didn\rquote t seem nervous about accepting his hand in hers. This small shift in her behavior made him feel very happy.\par
They walked hand in hand down the familiar path, chatting about the usual things; what they were up to that day, the new installment of the newspaper\rquote s mystery novel, and their plans for the summer.\par
Soon dusk fell. The forest quickly grew dark, and Kyle drew on the darkness to muster more courage.\par
Squeezing her hand, he yanked on her arm. She lost her balance for a moment, then stabled herself by resting her back against the trunk of a large tree on the side of the path. He stood facing her. The whole maneuver happened in a flash, but to him, it felt like an eternity.\par
\ldblquote Kyle?\rdblquote  she said in a faint, shaky voice. The scarlet color of her lips was visible even in the dusk.\par
He shut his eyes tightly and, gathering all his courage, leaned towards her. Right away he could feel her warm skin against his lips. But strangely, the sensation was different from what he had expected.\par
\par
He opened his eyes, and burst into laughter at what he saw. He had just kissed the back of her hand. She was looking at him with her hand held firmly over her mouth, blushing.\par
\ldblquote This kind of thing feels strange to me, Kyle,\rdblquote  she mumbled. \ldblquote If we do this kind of thing, it feels like we\rquote re doing something bad, and I don\rquote t\'85\rdblquote  Trailing off, she lowered her eyes. Her long, blonde eyelashes pointed downward.\par
You don\rquote t think what you\rquote re doing is even worse? he wanted to ask her, but he restrained himself, clearing his throat instead. His cheeks were just as red as hers. \ldblquote Miss Llewellyn, if you don\rquote t know how to kiss, what do you know?\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote Huh?\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote On the train, you were acting like you were an expert on everything.\rdblquote  \ldblquote What does that\'85 ah.\rdblquote  After a moment, she recalled their conversation in\par
which he had said he would jump off the moving train if she kept talking about reproductive behavior. \ldblquote Well that\rquote s\'85\rdblquote  She searched for the right words for a moment, then gave up and muttered the phrase she always used when she couldn\rquote t come up with a retort: \ldblquote I don\rquote t know about that.\rdblquote\par
He slumped into a resigned posture and let out a gentle sigh. He thought it was pitiful that he hadn\rquote t even kissed the woman he was going to marry, but he wasn\rquote t excessively upset about it. More than a kiss, what he really wanted was to win her heart. He wasn\rquote t going to let himself get swept up by passion if it was going to hurt her.\par
He put his hands to her cheeks and gently caressed them, then put his warm lips on her smooth forehead. He resolved not to be too demanding with her when it came to displays of affection.\par
He took a deep breath in, and the sweet smell of roses filled his lungs. It was Layla\rquote s scent.\par
