Even after opening her eyes, Layla lay still on her bed, staring at the ceiling. Her room was full of bright light, and the birds living in the trees by her window were singing just as brightly.\par
As each of her bleary senses grew alert, the cruel reality that she had forgotten during her illness came back to her as well. And yet it was strange\emdash  the clearer this reality became in her mind, the more peaceful her heart felt. It was as if all those excruciating emotions, which had made it hard even to breathe, had flowed out of her along with the sweat and tears she had shed while sick.\par
Two, no, three days had passed. After calculating how long she had spent in bed, she slowly sat up. She felt some dizziness for a moment, but it passed.\par
I\rquote ll have to wash these sheets. I should also dust the window frames, and re-wash the dishes that Uncle Bill tried to wash, and\'85\par
Thinking of all the tasks she would need to do, she felt overwhelmed and closed her eyes. When she opened them again, she decided on one task that needed to take precedence over all others.\par
She needed to see Kyle.\par
