It was an especially hot, muggy day, but Layla\rquote s outfit was almost stiflingly neat and tidy, from the stiffly-pressed collar of her blouse, which was buttoned all the way up, to her smooth, unwrinkled skirt and stockings. Even under the scorching afternoon sun, she looked perfect. Her cheeks were flushed and she was out of breath from the heat, but she kept a straight posture as she walked, even once she was no longer in anyone\rquote s sight.\par
Lately, wherever she went, she was greeted with looks of sympathy. Everyone who saw her rushed over to console her and criticize Mrs. Ettman.\par
\par
