When she passed people she knew in the city, their faces seemed to be offering similar advice.\par
Their expressions made her feel gratitude mixed with shame. Thus, she just greeted them courteously with a smile. Each time she did so, she noticed a slight smile appear on their lips as well, but she tried not to think about it. Fortunately, she was too busy maintaining her clean-cut appearance and smile to worry about anything else.\par
After consoling Layla for a long while, the teacher sighed again and said, \ldblquote I wish I could do something more for you, considering your situation, but this is the best I can osier right now.\rdblquote\par
All the positions for new teachers at schools in Karlsbar were already filled. The best option available to Layla was at a school in a small town about an hour away from Karlsbar by train.\par
After much deliberation, Layla finally accepted the position. Commuting each day would be too much, so she would have to find a boarding house to stay at during the week, but she would be able to return to Arvis on weekends. After teaching there for a year, there would probably be an open position in Karlsbar, and she would be able to move back.\par
\par
After arriving in front of Arvis\rquote s magnificent gate, she took off her hat and took a moment to catch her breath.\par
More than anyone else, she had had a hard time dealing with Uncle Bill. When she smiled, he would get a sad look in his eyes. Thus, she knew she certainly couldn\rquote t cry in front of him. Today she had good news, however, so perhaps it would be all right.\par
Cautiously holding on to that hope, she continued walking. It was a little sad that she would be going to a school in a distant location, but it wasn\rquote t like she was leaving Bill permanently.\par
She tried to smile more brightly as she increased her pace. Wanting to tell Bill the news right away, she skipped the cottage and went straight to the garden. As she entered the rose garden and passed under the archway, she ran into Kyle. \ldblquote Kyle\'85?\rdblquote  Her eyes widened with shock.\par
