Kyle left for the capital sooner than originally planned. The reason given was that he had a lot of preparation to do in the capital before classes began, but no one believed that excuse.\par
On the morning of his departure, Layla woke up earlier than usual. Hearing the sound of a bird cooing, she turned her head towards the window and saw Phoebe.\par
She put her glasses on, slowly walked to the window, and opened it wide. There was a note tied to Phoebe\rquote s ankle. Since Phoebe was trained to carry notes between her and Kyle\rquote s rooms, she knew who the note was from without having to look.\par
After hesitating for a moment, she took the note and unfurled it. Layla, I\rquote m leaving for the capital today.\par
Like a coward, I\rquote m going to the place that I was supposed to go with you.\par
I\rquote m not going to He and say that this is the best thing for you and me. When you get down to it, I\rquote m running away. I\rquote m turning away from the mess that real life has become and leaving you behind. Like a coward, I\rquote m pretending that what you said is true, that everything will be all right.\par
I\rquote m sorry. I\rquote m well aware that saying sorry won\rquote t wash away your wounds, but I still want to say it. I\rquote m sorry for the pain my mom caused you, and I\rquote m sorry that I wasn\rquote t able to stop her. I hurt you by naively thinking that everything could be fixed easily. I\rquote m only now realizing that.\par
\par
