\ldblquote That\rquote s right. We\rquote re just here to make sure you\rquote re doing okay,\rdblquote  said one of them.\par
\ldblquote Yes. You know, they say first loves never work out. I\rquote m sure you\rquote ll meet another man way better than Ky\emdash\rdblquote\par
\par
\ldblquote Oh my, look at the time!\rdblquote  Mona said, cutting the second maid off before she could say something that might make Layla feel bad. \ldblquote We\rquote d better get back to the mansion. We\rquote ve got to get ready for Lady Herhardt\rquote s teatime.\rdblquote\par
Layla said goodbye, then carried the heavy basket back to the kitchen. She took the cookies and cupcakes out one at a time, then suddenly froze. There was a cookie with peach jam on it, Kyle\rquote s favorite.\par
She stared across the table at the seat where Kyle had always used to sit. The days when the three of them would sit around the table were gone and would never return. All those meals where they enjoyed delicious food and boisterous conversation under the warm light of the lamp, they were now a thing of the past.\par
After staring at the empty chair for a moment longer, she snapped out of her daze, and quickly finished taking the treats out of the basket. Then, grabbing her hat and her old bag, she hurried out the back door and set off towards the forest path.\par
\ldblquote Fennel\'85 Baby\rquote s breath\'85 Butterfly bush\'85\rdblquote  She whispered the names of the flowers growing by the path as she walked. \ldblquote Linnet\'85 Swallowtail\'85 Grasshopper\'85\rdblquote  She also whispered the names of the birds and insects she saw. The odds and ends in her bag clinked rhythmically in accompaniment to the singsong sound of her whispering.\par
She walked and walked, and finally stopped in front of a large tree growing next to the Schulter River. She climbed up the tree, almost like she was hiding. Sitting on a sturdy branch high up on the thick trunk, she gazed at the blue water serenely flowing down below.\par
The sunlight shimmered on the water dazzlingly.\par
