Matthias swam back to the cabin, got dressed, and left. The color of the sunset was deepening, but Layla was still sitting in the tree, crying. She\par
still had not noticed his presence.\par
He stopped in front of the tree. After a while longer, she finally noticed him. But unlike on previous occasions, she didn\rquote t flinch or look away. Nor did she seem scared or on guard.\par
Matthias wondered at this for a moment, then the reason presented itself to him- her eyes were pointed at him, but she wasn\rquote t looking at him. Her unfocused gaze seemed to be pointed somewhere far away, perhaps at the place where the doctor\rquote s son was.\par
As Matthias started to grin, her gaze regained its focus. As her green eyes took in his face, they filled with confusion. Her face stiffened and her shoulders hunched. That was the Layla Llewellyn that he knew.\par
\par
Looking at her moist eyes, he crossed his arms. It was a leisurely evening. There was nothing he needed to hurry back for, and there was no reason why he couldn\rquote t wait for her. A look of alarm spread over her face as she realized that he had no intention of leaving. This made him laugh. \ldblquote He\rquote s not coming, Layla. You know that, don\rquote t you?\rdblquote  He took a step towards the tree. \ldblquote Kyle Ettman. The boy you\rquote re waiting for. Ah. Perhaps I should call him the boy who abandoned you?\rdblquote  Staring straight into her eyes, he smiled. His voice remained soft and gentle even as he said these piercing words.\par
Smiling hollowly, she looked up and saw that the birds had left the dusky sky. The scenery seemed to swell as she gazed at it until tears formed and started to flow down her cheeks.\par
Without saying anything in response to him, she started chewing on her lip. She realized that if she waited for that cruel man to leave, she might have to stay up in the tree until late at night.\par
She climbed down the back side of the tree, where he couldn\rquote t see. She felt some vertigo, perhaps because of all the tears she had shed, but luckily she made it safely to the ground without an accident.\par
Leaning against the tree, she lifted her apron and wiped her tears. Then she neatened her disheveled hair and stood up straight. After that, she went around to the other side of the tree. The duke was still blocking the path that led back to the cottage.\par
Rather than slipping around the side of him, she started to approach him, one step at a time. Her tears continued to flow, soon wetting her whole face again, but she didn\rquote t care. She knew she couldn\rquote t hide the tears, so she wore them with pride. She didn\rquote t want to be reduced to his plaything. \ldblquote I\rquote m sorry for my rudeness,\rdblquote  she said. \ldblquote I\rquote ll be going now. Goodbye, Your Grace.\rdblquote  Standing about two paces away from him, she curtsied with utmost politeness. By now,\par
\par
displaying the formalities that aristocrats expected was as natural to her as breathing.\par
Just as she was about to brush past him, he said, \ldblquote Layla.\rdblquote  She flinched but didn\rquote t stop.\par
\ldblquote Layla Llewellyn,\rdblquote  he said, laughing as he turned around. She kept walking onward as if she couldn\rquote t hear him.\par
He frowned, feeling that she was being unacceptably rude. Just then, she suddenly tripped and fell. Her shoulders and back trembled intermittently as she sat slumped on the ground, crying.\par
Clicking his tongue, he slowly approached her. That strong-willed girl, whose eyes maintained their look of bold independence even while they were shedding tears, was now sobbing on the ground in an undignified posture.\par
Squinting, he went down on one knee in front of her and picked up her glasses. She barely lifted her head. Her tears, which had brought him so much joy in the past, no longer did so.\par
Seeing her cry because of Kyle Ettman gave him a feeling that it took him a moment to identify: humiliation. It was a feeling he had never before experienced.\par
\ldblquote Don\rquote t cry,\rdblquote  he quietly said, grabbing her chin.\par
She tried to turn her head away, but she couldn\rquote t overcome his fierce grip. \ldblquote Let go!\rdblquote  she shouted, struggling to free herself.\par
\ldblquote Don\rquote t cry,\rdblquote  he calmly repeated. Ignoring her resistance, he was easily able to dominate her with one hand.\par
\ldblquote Don\rquote t you enjoy seeing me cry?\rdblquote  she asked in frustration. The feeling of indignation that his inescapable grip was giving her caused her tears to flow even more.\par
\par
\ldblquote Since when have you been interested in what I enjoy?\rdblquote  he asked, chuckling at the sight of her sniffling. \ldblquote I thought you hated it when I enjoyed things.\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote No,\rdblquote  she replied, trying to hold back her tears and weakly shaking her head while he maintained his grip on her chin.\par
\ldblquote Whether you enjoy things or not has nothing to do with me. Just like my tears have nothing to do with you.\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote Oh, but Layla, they do have to do with me.\rdblquote  He cocked his head. \ldblquote Don\rquote t cry,\rdblquote  he said again, looking at her with a gentle expression.\par
\ldblquote Do I need your permission to cry?\rdblquote  she scoffed. \ldblquote Maybe you do.\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote What do you mean? You don\rquote t have that right.\rdblquote  \ldblquote That right\'85?\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote Just because you\rquote re the owner of Arvis doesn\rquote t mean you own me.\rdblquote  \ldblquote Really?\rdblquote  He frowned for an instant before smiling again. \ldblquote Then shall I take\par
you for myself now?\rdblquote  The smile quickly faded, leaving his face blank and expressionless, like still water.\par
Her lips started to quiver with fear.\par
\ldblquote That way, I\rquote ll be your owner.\rdblquote  He put his finger to her lips.\par
She shuddered as the sensation brought back her memory of when he had touched her lips the previous summer. Her heart, which had been filled with sadness over losing Kyle, suddenly froze. \ldblquote No.\rdblquote  Unable to stand the thought of being sprawled out at his feet anymore, she used all her strength to lift her upper body from the ground.\par
He let go of her at once and stood up, like a child who had grown tired of a\par
\par
toy.\par
Enveloped by his shadow, she staggered to her feet. Her face was messy\par
\par
with dirt and tears, but her eyes remained strong. \ldblquote To think that you, a duke\'85\par
\par
a duke with a fiancee\'85 would behave in such a dishonorable way\'85 I don\rquote t like it at all.\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote So?\rdblquote  he asked, fiddling with her glasses, which he was still holding. \ldblquote What do your feelings have to do with me?\rdblquote  There was no hostility in his voice. \ldblquote I want you.\rdblquote\par
What he wanted, he got; it was as simple as that. He wanted Layla Llewellyn, so he was going to have her. He needed to discard her so that his life could be complete again, but he knew he couldn\rquote t discard her unless he first had her.\par
He gently put her glasses back on her stunned face. \ldblquote Go.\rdblquote  As he drew his hand away from her face, she collapsed to the ground again.\par
He gazed down at her for a short while, then proceeded to stroll alongside the river.\par
She remained in the same spot long after he was out of sight.\par
