It came as no surprise to anyone that the Herhardt family\rquote s banquet was perfect. The duke\rquote s mother and grandmother played their joint hostess roles perfectly as well. In the Berg Empire, the name Herhardt was synonymous with perfection. If something were ever to go wrong at a Herhardt banquet, it would only increase everyone\rquote s fervent enjoyment.\par
\ldblquote Is it all right if we go for a stroll in the greenhouse?\rdblquote  Claudine asked just as it was becoming time to move to the drawing room for conversation. Her fiance stood on one side of her and her cousin on the other.\par
\ldblquote Of course, go ahead,\rdblquote  Elise von Herhardt replied. \ldblquote You young people need some time to yourselves too.\rdblquote\par
The noblewomen around her laughed in response to her subtle tone.\par
As the older ladies began to gossip about young people\rquote s love lives, Claudine, Matthias, and Riette left the drawing room.\par
\ldblquote Oh, Duke Herhardt, Dowager Herhardt told me today that I\rquote m free to expand the greenhouse once I become duchess,\rdblquote  Claudine said. The bright\par
\par
sound of her voice permeated the dim, quiet greenhouse.\par
\ldblquote I see,\rdblquote  Matthias replied, a slight smile forming on his lips. \ldblquote How do you feel about that?\rdblquote  she asked.\par
\ldblquote I think you should do whatever you like.\rdblquote\par
It was exactly the response she had expected, but she still nodded cheerfully. \ldblquote You should look forward to it, then. I\rquote m going to put my heart and soul into the project, as is only fitting for Arvis\rquote s heaven.\rdblquote\par
She strolled down the greenhouse\rquote s walking path with light steps. Her fiance Matthias was escorting her, but she mostly conversed with the more talkative Riette, as always.\par
Just as she was starting to talk about the tropical flowers she was going to cultivate in the expanded greenhouse, a servant appeared, looking for Matthias. It seemed that someone needed to have a business discussion with the duke.\par
\ldblquote Hurry back,\rdblquote  Claudine said as she let go of her fiance\rquote s arm. \ldblquote Riette and I will continue our walk.\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote I always end up acting as Duke Herhardt\rquote s pinch hitter with you, Lady Claudine,\rdblquote  Riette playfully grumbled as he offered his arm to Claudine.\par
Matthias and the servant left, leaving Claudine and Riette alone amid the babbling sound of the greenhouse\rquote s fountain.\par
They resumed their conversation as they slowly walked. Her plans for the expansion of the greenhouse were quite detailed. She already knew exactly which flowers she was going to import and where she was going to put them.\par
\ldblquote It seems like you\rquote re already Duchess Herhardt at heart. And it seems like your love for your fiance is exceeded by your love for Arvis,\rdblquote  Riette remarked with a smile.\par
\par
Claudine nodded without a hint of shame. \ldblquote One way or the other, it\rquote s all love for the Herhardt family, isn\rquote t it?\rdblquote  she replied.\par
\ldblquote The two of you are quite impressive,\rdblquote  he said in a defeated tone, chuckling. \ldblquote Are you really all right with the way Matthias is? He\rquote s always been like that.\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote I don\rquote t know what you\rquote re talking about, Riette.\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote He doesn\rquote t love you at all. He never has, and he never will.\rdblquote  \ldblquote Are there any prestigious nobles who marry for love?\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote It happens. It would happen if you were to marry me and become Marchioness Lindman.\rdblquote  His face and voice remained casual as always.\par
She smiled in response to his comment, then said, \ldblquote Riette, I\rquote ve been coming here to Arvis with my mother for the past ten years.\rdblquote  She turned to face him. \ldblquote You know what that means, don\rquote t you?\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote Yes, it means that for the past ten years, the nobles of this empire have already thought of you as Duchess Herhardt.\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote That\rquote s right. That\rquote s what I like about you \emdash you always get it.\rdblquote  Giggling quietly, she linked arms with him again.\par
He casually started leading her forward again. The subtle tension between them soon disappeared amidst their laughter.\par
\ldblquote Also, when I expand the greenhouse, I want to raise a peacock,\rdblquote  she said as they passed in front of the greenhouse\rquote s colorful birds.\par
\ldblquote Be careful. The duke has a thing for birds \emdash if you get such a beautiful bird, he might fall in love,\rdblquote  Riette replied in an uncharacteristically sarcastic tone.\par
\ldblquote Riette!\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote By the way, I noticed that he still has that bird. The pretty little one in his bedroom.\rdblquote\par
\par
\ldblquote I don\rquote t mind. Even he needs his small pleasures.\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote I pray that it won\rquote t progress beyond the level of a small pleasure.\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote Save your prayers, Riette. A bird can\rquote t become a duchess, no matter how pretty.\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote Well, sure,\rdblquote  he replied, unable to refute her point this time. No matter how fond Matthias was of the canary, it was just a bird. \ldblquote But how long do canaries live? A long time?\rdblquote\par
She cocked her head as they walked around a curve in the path. \ldblquote I certainly hope that noisy bird doesn\rquote t live too long.\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote I thought you respected the duke\rquote s need for small pleasures.\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote I do, but once that bird is gone, another bird can become his new pleasure.\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote I must say, Claudine, it\rquote s times like these that I want to give you and Matthias my sincere blessings.\rdblquote  Gazing at her face, he gave a hollow smile. \ldblquote You\rquote re such a perfect couple.\rdblquote\par
He suddenly felt vaguely sorry for the duke\rquote s little bird. Thinking of how it was doomed to flutter around that perfect couple, he felt a sense of kinship with it.\par
Claudine flashed a natural smile. Gazing at her cruel yet beautiful face, Riette blurted, \ldblquote Shall I try to get to know that bird, for my precious cousin?\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote I didn\rquote t know you were interested in birds, Riette.\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote They\rquote re not normally my thing, but that one is just so pretty, you know?\rdblquote  \ldblquote It won\rquote t be easy,\rdblquote  she replied, laughing with genuine interest now. \ldblquote That\par
bird is pretty, but she has the temperament of a princess.\rdblquote  \ldblquote You underestimate me, Lady Claudine.\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote I certainly do not. I was just letting you know what you\rquote re up against. I wonder, will you be able to become close with that arrogant bird?\rdblquote  No longer\par
\par
smiling, the expression on her face now looked as cold as the greenhouse walls through which the moonlight was shining. \ldblquote If you succeed, I\rquote ll be sure to send you a congratulatory\par
\ldblquote What sort of gift?\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote Would my thanks and love be sufficient?\rdblquote  she replied, lightly squeezing his arm.\par
After the affected smiles left their faces, they gazed at each other more solemnly.\par
\ldblquote Sure, that\rquote ll do,\rdblquote  he quietly replied.\par
Just then, the greenhouse\rquote s door opened again.\par
They started slowly walking toward Duke Herhardt.\par
